Z||000000||skitime||01-14-2001||11:31 PM||||I was at a yard and saw a coupe (year unknown0. The trunk lid had louvers that went from one removable engine vent to the other removable one and was about the same width as the side vents. I have only had GTs so maybe this is normal for some year but I am not familiar with it.  Does anyone have one of these and if you do could you post a picture of it. ||||reg||1
Z||000001||theogre||01-14-2001||11:51 PM||||sounds like an 84. they are the only ones with a factory vent grate in the lid.||||reg||1
Z||000002||Will||01-14-2001||11:52 PM||||That was an '84. In stock form, the panels that are vents on the later cars are just blanked off and smooth. Putting the two setups together is a good way to improve engine compartment ventilation.||||reg||1
Z||000003||Mi Junk||01-14-2001||11:53 PM||||You were looking at a 84. 84's had a big center vent made of magnesium. <BR>I don't have any pics for you, just my useless bits of knowledge... so my wife says.<P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/85_sig_2.jpg"> ||||reg||6
